        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2023-02-13T20:33:31.887Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "62117114e5cc0010fbd1e0f3",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "What about drama from years ago preventing a player from inviting a friend over to even private instances? I don't want drama between someone I don't even know and a friend, or friend's friend to have to make me swap worlds or have to exclude somebody. I can understand for a semi-public group-controlled instances to have perma-bans. I do however think whatever system of control should be put in place to create the environment for good moderation shouldn't extend outside of user's instances. I think if we had instances that could be public but controlled via group role permissions and bans. That could sidestep the core issue I have with this idea, while also barring jerks from just popping in again later.\n\nI think that would be the best way to avoid the most issues. And while I get some may feel the desire to say \"No! I want them banned from entering the world itself. Whether I'm there or not.\" I feel that this comes more out of spite, than an actually desire to avoid conflict. That's ultimately what I want. A low-conflict solution.\n\nEdit: Oh and I forget to add. What about worlds created by several creators? What if they disagree about another player? I've seen many a set of friends have a falling out only for the mutuals to be stuck in the crossfire. Just another point of contention.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
