      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f8a26770aaa28611fedd6b6|full_name}: Then permit me to convey it. Furhub moderators are aware of a small number of users who engage in groups bypassing EAC, create and share crasher avatars, and bypass bans with over 100 alt accounts. These people make VRChat unsafe and problematic for everyone. Everyone who has enough friends knows to stay away from public instances because of the hell that keeps happening.\n\nWhen the Virtual Furry Museum first went public, I was hoping to join public instances to give people tours. But out of 2,940 visits within the last 23 days, checking every day, hardly any public instances were created that I could join. Everyone chose to visit the museum in private, even my friends. The few public instances I started got a decent crowd, but very few people who weren't already my friend \n\nor a friend of a friend joined. In one such public instance, the same group of people described by Furhub moderators wore an avatar blocking people's views. I let him know his avatar disrupted other people and I asked him to change it. He refused. I told him if he can't do that, I'll have to remove him from the instance, and he claimed I was breaking VRChat's ToS, apparently, for using the moderation tools that come with the game. He was kicked, and his friends smeared me behind my back.\n\nPeople have stopped traveling to public instances because of the repeated behavior and harassment of a small group. Bans should be made technically impossible for anyone to evade. There should be a way to apply such bans to all accounts unilaterally. If VR Chat's centralized ToS team can't do it, then we need the ability to stop them ourselves. The tools we have aren't enough, and the collective psyche of VRC players has already assumed the worst. Now I created a world that would be amazing if people used it safely publicly. But I can't recommend people do that if this keeps happening. The best I can do is inform people about the current tools, and they're far from enough to deal with this.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-02-19T22:37:08.492Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRC's choke hold of the ability to ban users is in every possible way, disgusting mislead and mismanaged. \nThis is a feature that should be allowed to world creators / owners. the argument against giving this option to users is empty as can be. \nVRC staff refuses to investigate reports in a timely manner, not allowing world owner/ creator to ban problematic people allows people actively breaking TOS and world rules to continue doing so. \nThey continue to harrass others , crash worlds , grief, sexually assault , etc. other players.  Blocking is not a acceptable replacement when alt accounts can be made in a manner of seconds. \nThere is no acceptable reason to deny world owners / creators the ability to deny access to their world to those wishing to cause trouble in it. \nallowing a owner / creator to ban also is not , \"denial of service\" as any individual can create a new instance of any world to go into themselves. From what I witnessed the only way to do a ban was to use a mod that allowed banning which VRC has since banned .  You have banned a mod allowing people to ban problematic users that your staff refuses to handle while refusing to give the option to ban. \nTo make a apt metaphor , If someone walks into your home and shoots you , you actively claim that person has every right to walk into your home and shoot you but you have no right to tell them they are not allowed to enter uninvited nor allowed to defend yourself. \nplease ad the ban option for world owner / creator / master.  Or explain the ethics behind the decision to allow individuals to cause havock while staff refuses to handle reports on them .",
